.TH GLEDITOR 1 "2026" "gleditor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gleditor \- GPU-rendered text editor with OpenGL, OpenGL ES and Vulkan backends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gleditor
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gleditor
draws text on the GPU. Documents are laid out as pages in a 3D scene, shaped
and rasterised with Pango and Cairo, and drawn as instanced quads sampled from
a glyph atlas.
.PP
One rendering pipeline serves three graphics APIs, selected at run time with
.BR \-\-backend .
Everything above the backend is written against a single device interface and
names no graphics API.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " NAME"
Rendering backend:
.BR opengl " (default), " opengles " or " vulkan .
The Vulkan backend is only present when the binary was built with it.
.TP
.BI \-\-font " DESCRIPTION"
Default font, as a Pango font description, for example
.BR """Serif 16""" .
.TP
.BI \-\-fov " DEGREES"
Initial vertical field of view. Widening it is how several pages are brought
on screen at once.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cull
Draw every page of every document, including those entirely outside the view.
Only useful for checking that culling changes nothing it should not.
.TP
.BI \-\-coarse\-below " SCALE"
Draw a page as one solid bar per line once one layout pixel of it covers fewer
than
.I SCALE
screen pixels. Zero draws every visible page in full detail.
.TP
.BI \-\-benchmark " N"
Draw
.I N
frames once the document has settled, then report frame, collect and record
times and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " PATH"
Write the first fully drawn frame to
.I PATH
as a binary PPM.
.TP
.BI \-\-pick " X,Y"
Report the picking tag at a pixel once the document has settled. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-click " X,Y"
Click at a pixel once the document has settled, placing the caret. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-select " START,END"
Select the document byte range once the document has settled.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " TEXT"
Insert text at the caret once it has been placed.
.TP
.BI \-\-toast " SEVERITY:MESSAGE"
Show a notification once the first frame is drawn. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-diagnostics
Treat a driver error as fatal instead of showing it as a notification, and set
the exit status accordingly. Automated runs want this: a frame rendered by a
driver that was reporting errors proves nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-profile
Perform initial setup, then quit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-present
Draw frames without showing them. For capturing a frame on a machine that can
give a rendering context but cannot put one on a screen, such as a headless
Windows runner, where the frame is drawn correctly and the software driver then
fails inside the call that puts it on screen. The capture is unaffected:
drawing goes to an offscreen target either way. Accepted by the OpenGL and
OpenGL ES backends; the Vulkan backend refuses it, because every frame acquires
a swapchain image and presenting is what returns it.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-asset\-dir
Report the directory the shaders and icon were found in, then quit without
opening a window. Answers the one question a package can be asked on a machine
whose driver cannot give it a context, and pairs with
.B GLEDITOR_ASSET_DIR
below.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GLEDITOR_ASSET_DIR
Directory holding the shaders and the window icon. Set this only when they are
somewhere the usual search will not find them; it is taken as given rather than
checked, so a wrong value reports itself as a missing shader.
.TP
.B GLEDITOR_ATLAS_SIZE
Side length the glyph atlas opens at before it grows to fit. Exists so that
atlas growth can be exercised, since no ordinary document provokes it.
.TP
.B GLEDITOR_RECORD_THREADS
Threads the Vulkan backend records a frame with. An instruction rather than a
ceiling: setting it takes the choice away from the device, so
.B 1
records in one piece and anything more always splits. Ignored by the other
backends, which cannot split.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/shaders
Portable shader bodies, and the SPIR-V built from them.
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/logo.png
Window icon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success. Non-zero when the render thread stopped because of an error
rather than because it was asked to, which includes a driver diagnostic under
.BR \-\-strict\-diagnostics .
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README, which documents the rendering pipeline and the
measurements behind it, at
.UR https://github.com/ccs4ever/gleditor
.UE .
